A computer is an electronic machine that accepts raw data,
processes it according to software instructions,
and outputs useful information.


Core Components

• Hardware: The physical parts you can touch, including:
	• Central Processing Unit (CPU): The "brain" that executes calculations and instructions.
	• Memory (RAM): Temporary, fast storage that holds active programs while the machine is on.
	• Storage (SSD / HDD): Permanent space for saving your operating system, files, and apps.
	• Input/Output Devices: Tools like a keyboard and mouse for input, and a monitor or printer for output.